{"kind":"assert","text":"Two dispositions: gate attempt 2 (`86142777`) and the descriptor\naudit (`9616652e`).\n\nGate attempt 2. One Native case of 1,174 failed after 1,807 s: the\naggregate-limit expectation of `archive-inventory.test.ts` still\nholds 64 nodes. The repair is yours. Three conditions for attempt 3:\n\n1. The expectation takes its value from the shared definition, as\n   the reader does. A literal copy is the fault that this head\n   repairs.\n2. Before START, search the test sources and the fixtures at the\n   exact head for the old values in each written form: 64 nodes,\n   67108864, and the product form of 64 MiB. Put the result in the\n   START act: each hit, and why it stays or changes.\n3. Before START, run whole each Native owner that reads a\n   serialized inventory or its ceilings, and not only the nine\n   archive owners. The first set missed this owner, and that cost\n   one gate. Name the owners and their counts in the START act.\n\nThe Node condition of `7be10b34` stands for attempt 3.\n\nDescriptor digest. The fixture of `c4-replica-explore.test.ts` is a\nstand-in, and no step has built the real descriptor. C4 compiles as\nplanned, with two limits:\n\n4. The fixture passes a constant that its name marks as a test\n   value. It does not hash `dap.application.json` or a path text,\n   so no reader takes it for the rule of the digest.\n5. C4 treats the digest as an opaque value and compares it only for\n   equality. C4 writes no rule for what the digest covers.\n\nThe rule belongs to the step that builds the descriptor, and I file\nit as a request: the digest covers the content of section 10 for\nthe definition of the scope, and no version text, name or path. A\nrelease that changes no act of a scope keeps the digest of that\nscope, and one test pins that.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}